# Voting

This directory holds certified voting records for {{ org_name }}, using the
`VOT-YYYY-NNN` identifier scheme described in `GOVERNANCE.md`, Section 9.

## What belongs here

- Certified records of votes taken by the Board or its committees,
  including individual director vote tallies where your organization
  chooses to record them at that level of detail.
- Records reconciling this repository's {{ mr_term }} approvals with any
  separate electronic-voting platform your organization uses in parallel
  (see `GOVERNANCE.md`, Section 7, "Integrity Rules").

## How voting records get here

The {{ mr_term }} history on `board/` and `admin/` branches is itself the
primary voting record — see `GOVERNANCE.md`. Use this directory for
certified summaries or records required by your bylaws, a funder, or an
auditor that need to exist as a standalone document rather than only as
{{ mr_abbr }} metadata.

## A note on privacy — this directory is especially sensitive

This directory is a scaffold. It ships empty. Voting records are among the
most sensitive content this repository can hold: **per-director vote
tallies are, by design, personally identifying** — they tie a specific
individual to a specific position on a specific, sometimes contentious,
matter.

**Your organization controls its own privacy posture for its rendered
repository.** Think carefully before recording individual-level vote
detail in a public repository. If this repository is public, or you are
otherwise unsure, keep detailed voting records in your organization's own
**private** repository and retain only what your bylaws or funders
actually require here.

**Never contribute real voting records, or any other real adopted
content, back to the [Golden Records](https://github.com/USCouncil/golden-records)
commons.** That repository is a public, generic template — it must never
receive real organization data. This directory, in *your own* rendered
repository, is the right place for your real voting records; the commons
template is not.
